{number: 143}
{title: Under His Wings}
{key: Db}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Db] Under His wings I am safely a-[Gb] biding,
Though the night [Db] deepens and tempests are [Ab7] wild,
Still [Db] I can trust Him; I know He will [Gb] keep me,
He has re-[Db] deemed me, and [Ab7] I am His [Db] child.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Under His [Gb] wings, under His [Db] wings,
Who from His [Ab7] love can sever?
Under His [Db] wings my soul shall a-[Gb] bide,
Safely a-[Db] bide for-[Ab7] ever. [Db]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Db] Under His wings, what a refuge in [Gb] sorrow!
How the heart [Db] yearns for the blessing of [Ab7] rest!
Unto [Db] the cross I have fled for pro-[Gb] tection,
Pardon and [Db] peace I have [Ab7] found in His [Db] breast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Db] Under His wings, oh, what precious en-[Gb] joyment!
There will I [Db] hide till life's trials are [Ab7] o'er;
Sheltered, [Db] protected, no evil can [Gb] harm me,
Resting in [Db] Jesus for-[Ab7] ever-[Db] more.
{end_of_verse}
